   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Literal Pattern Matching\n",
    "\n",
    "Literal patterns match exact strings. They are:\n",
    "- Fast and efficient\n",
    "- Case-sensitive by default\n",
    "- Best for known, fixed error messages\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example: OOM Killer Detection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.matching.pattern_matcher import LiteralPatternMatcher\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a literal pattern matcher\n",
    "oom_matcher = LiteralPatternMatcher(pattern=\"oom-kill event\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test it on sample lines\n",
    "test_lines = [\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:20:45] ERROR: Out of memory - slurmstepd: error: Detected 1 oom-kill event\",\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:20:46] SLURM: Job 12345 FAILED with exit code 137\",\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:15:00] WARNING: Memory usage at 75% threshold\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Testing literal pattern: 'oom-kill event'\\n\")\n",
    "for line in test_lines:\n",
    "    match = oom_matcher.match(line)\n",
    "    status = \"✓ MATCH\" if match else \"✗ No match\"\n",
    "    print(f\"{status}: {line[:60]}...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Literal Pattern in Catalog"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "literal_catalog = {\n",
    "    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n",
    "    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n",
    "    \"metadata\": {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"Literal Pattern Example\",\n",
    "        \"description\": \"Demonstrates literal pattern matching\",\n",
    "        \"author\": \"Tutorial\",\n",
    "        \"created\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
    "        \"updated\": datetime.now().isoformat()\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"errors\": {\n",
    "        \"oom_killer\": {\n",
    "            \"id\": \"oom_killer\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": {\n",
    "                \"type\": \"literal\",\n",
    "                \"pattern\": \"oom-kill event\"  # Exact string to match\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"*.log\")],\n",
    "            \"meaning\": \"Process killed by Linux OOM killer due to memory exhaustion\",\n",
    "            \"suggestion\": \"Increase job memory allocation or optimize memory usage\",\n",
    "            \"context_lines\": 3,\n",
    "            \"next_errors\": [],\n",
    "            \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"critical\"}\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(yaml.dump(literal_catalog['errors']['oom_killer']['pattern'], \n",
    "                default_flow_style=False, sort_keys=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Regex Pattern Matching\n",
    "\n",
    "Regex patterns use regular expressions for flexible matching. They support:\n",
    "- Pattern groups and capture\n",
    "- Case-insensitive matching\n",
    "- Multi-line patterns\n",
    "- Complex patterns with alternation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example: Connection Errors"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.matching.pattern_matcher import RegexPatternMatcher\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create regex pattern for connection errors\n",
    "conn_pattern = r\"Connection\\s+(timeout|failed|refused)\"\n",
    "conn_matcher = RegexPatternMatcher(\n",
    "    pattern=conn_pattern,\n",
    "    flags=[re.IGNORECASE]  # Case-insensitive\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test on sample lines\n",
    "test_lines = [\n",
    "    \"2024-01-15T08:15:30Z WARN Connection timeout after 30s (attempt 1/5)\",\n",
    "    \"2024-01-15T08:16:30Z ERROR Connection failed: Connection refused (errno: 111)\",\n",
    "    \"2024-01-15T09:00:00Z INFO Reconnection successful to remote.server.com:443\",\n",
    "    \"Connection REFUSED by server\"  # Tests case-insensitive\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Testing regex pattern: {conn_pattern}\\n\")\n",
    "for line in test_lines:\n",
    "    match = conn_matcher.match(line)\n",
    "    if match:\n",
    "        matches = conn_matcher.find_all(line)\n",
    "        print(f\"✓ MATCH: {line}\")\n",
    "        if matches:\n",
    "            print(f\"  → Captured: '{matches[0].matched_text}'\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"✗ No match: {line}\")\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Regex Pattern in Catalog"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "regex_catalog_entry = {\n",
    "    \"connection_errors\": {\n",
    "        \"id\": \"connection_errors\",\n",
    "        \"pattern\": {\n",
    "            \"type\": \"regex\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": r\"Connection\\s+(timeout|failed|refused)\",\n",
    "            \"flags\": [\"IGNORECASE\", \"MULTILINE\"]\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"*.log\")],\n",
    "        \"meaning\": \"Network connection error detected\",\n",
    "        \"suggestion\": \"Check network connectivity and firewall rules\",\n",
    "        \"context_lines\": 2,\n",
    "        \"next_errors\": [],\n",
    "        \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"network\"}\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Regex Pattern Configuration:\")\n",
    "print(yaml.dump(regex_catalog_entry['connection_errors']['pattern'], \n",
    "                default_flow_style=False, sort_keys=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Common Regex Flags\n",
    "\n",
    "| Flag | Description | Use Case |\n",
    "|------|-------------|----------|\n",
    "| `IGNORECASE` | Case-insensitive matching | Match \"ERROR\", \"error\", \"Error\" |\n",
    "| `MULTILINE` | `^` and `$` match line boundaries | Multi-line log entries |\n",
    "| `DOTALL` | `.` matches newlines | Patterns spanning multiple lines |\n",
    "| `VERBOSE` | Allow comments in regex | Complex patterns with documentation |\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Callable Pattern Matching\n",
    "\n",
    "Callable patterns use custom Python functions for complex logic. Use them when:\n",
    "- Regex patterns are too complex or slow\n",
    "- You need stateful matching\n",
    "- You need to parse structured data (JSON, XML)\n",
    "- You need arithmetic or logical operations\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example: Memory Threshold Detection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define a custom matcher function\n",
    "def high_memory_usage(line: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Detect memory usage above 80% threshold.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Parses lines like:\n",
    "    \"MEMORY: Process using 205.6 GB / 256.0 GB\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Returns True if usage percentage > 80%.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    import re\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Match pattern: \"X GB / Y GB\"\n",
    "    match = re.search(r'(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*GB\\s*/\\s*(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*GB', line)\n",
    "    if not match:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    \n",
    "    used = float(match.group(1))\n",
    "    total = float(match.group(2))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if total == 0:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    \n",
    "    percentage = (used / total) * 100\n",
    "    return percentage > 80.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test the function\n",
    "test_lines = [\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:10:15] MEMORY: Process using 128.4 GB / 256.0 GB\",  # 50%\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:15:00] WARNING: Memory usage at 75% threshold\",     # No match\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:20:00] MEMORY: Process using 205.6 GB / 256.0 GB\",  # 80.3%\n",
    "    \"[2024-01-15 10:22:00] MEMORY: Process using 240.0 GB / 256.0 GB\",  # 93.75%\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Testing callable pattern: high_memory_usage()\\n\")\n",
    "for line in test_lines:\n",
    "    match = high_memory_usage(line)\n",
    "    status = \"✓ MATCH (>80%)\" if match else \"✗ No match\"\n",
    "    print(f\"{status}: {line}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Callable Pattern in Catalog\n",
    "\n",
    "To use a callable pattern in a catalog, save your function in a Python module and reference it:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a custom matchers module\n",
    "matchers_file = tutorial_dir / \"custom_matchers.py\"\n",
    "matchers_file.write_text('''\n",
    "\"\"\"Custom pattern matchers for tutorial.\"\"\"\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "def high_memory_usage(line: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Detect memory usage above 80% threshold.\"\"\"\n",
    "    match = re.search(r'(\\\\d+\\\\.?\\\\d*)\\\\s*GB\\\\s*/\\\\s*(\\\\d+\\\\.?\\\\d*)\\\\s*GB', line)\n",
    "    if not match:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    \n",
    "    used = float(match.group(1))\n",
    "    total = float(match.group(2))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if total == 0:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    \n",
    "    percentage = (used / total) * 100\n",
    "    return percentage > 80.0\n",
    "\n",
    "def database_deadlock(line: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Detect database deadlock errors.\"\"\"\n",
    "    deadlock_keywords = ['deadlock', 'lock wait timeout', 'transaction rolled back']\n",
    "    line_lower = line.lower()\n",
    "    return any(keyword in line_lower for keyword in deadlock_keywords)\n",
    "''')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Created custom matchers module: {matchers_file}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Catalog entry using callable pattern\n",
    "callable_catalog_entry = {\n",
    "    \"high_memory\": {\n",
    "        \"id\": \"high_memory\",\n",
    "        \"pattern\": {\n",
    "            \"type\": \"callable\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": \"custom_matchers:high_memory_usage\"  # module:function\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"hpc_job.log\")],\n",
    "        \"meaning\": \"Memory usage exceeded 80% threshold\",\n",
    "        \"suggestion\": \"Monitor for potential OOM kills, consider increasing allocation\",\n",
    "        \"context_lines\": 2,\n",
    "        \"next_errors\": [\n",
    "            {\n",
    "                \"error_id\": \"oom_killer\",\n",
    "                \"when\": {\"type\": \"always\"}  # Check for OOM after high memory\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"warning\", \"category\": \"performance\"}\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCallable Pattern Configuration:\")\n",
    "print(yaml.dump(callable_catalog_entry['high_memory']['pattern'], \n",
    "                default_flow_style=False, sort_keys=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Complete Example: Multi-Pattern Catalog\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's create a comprehensive catalog using all three pattern types:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "complete_catalog = {\n",
    "    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n",
    "    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n",
    "    \"metadata\": {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"Multi-Pattern Catalog\",\n",
    "        \"description\": \"Demonstrates all three pattern types\",\n",
    "        \"author\": \"Tutorial\",\n",
    "        \"created\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
    "        \"updated\": datetime.now().isoformat()\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"errors\": {\n",
    "        # Literal pattern\n",
    "        \"oom_killer\": {\n",
    "            \"id\": \"oom_killer\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": {\n",
    "                \"type\": \"literal\",\n",
    "                \"pattern\": \"oom-kill event\"\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"*.log\")],\n",
    "            \"meaning\": \"Process killed by OOM killer\",\n",
    "            \"suggestion\": \"Increase memory allocation\",\n",
    "            \"context_lines\": 3,\n",
    "            \"next_errors\": [],\n",
    "            \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"critical\"}\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        # Regex pattern\n",
    "        \"connection_errors\": {\n",
    "            \"id\": \"connection_errors\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": {\n",
    "                \"type\": \"regex\",\n",
    "                \"pattern\": r\"Connection\\s+(timeout|failed|refused)\",\n",
    "                \"flags\": [\"IGNORECASE\"]\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"network.log\")],\n",
    "            \"meaning\": \"Network connection error\",\n",
    "            \"suggestion\": \"Check network and firewall\",\n",
    "            \"context_lines\": 2,\n",
    "            \"next_errors\": [],\n",
    "            \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"high\"}\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        # Callable pattern\n",
    "        \"database_deadlock\": {\n",
    "            \"id\": \"database_deadlock\",\n",
    "            \"pattern\": {\n",
    "                \"type\": \"callable\",\n",
    "                \"pattern\": \"custom_matchers:database_deadlock\"\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"files\": [str(logs_dir / \"database.log\")],\n",
    "            \"meaning\": \"Database deadlock detected\",\n",
    "            \"suggestion\": \"Review transaction isolation levels and query order\",\n",
    "            \"context_lines\": 2,\n",
    "            \"next_errors\": [],\n",
    "            \"metadata\": {\"severity\": \"medium\"}\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save catalog\n",
    "catalog_path = tutorial_dir / \"multi_pattern_catalog.yaml\"\n",
    "with open(catalog_path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    yaml.dump(complete_catalog, f, default_flow_style=False, sort_keys=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Complete catalog saved to: {catalog_path}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nCatalog contains {len(complete_catalog['errors'])} error definitions:\")\n",
    "for error_id, error_def in complete_catalog['errors'].items():\n",
    "    pattern_type = error_def['pattern']['type']\n",
    "    print(f\"  - {error_id}: {pattern_type} pattern\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern Matching Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "### When to Use Each Pattern Type\n",
    "\n",
    "| Pattern Type | Use When | Performance | Complexity |\n",
    "|--------------|----------|-------------|------------|\n",
    "| **Literal** | Exact string known | Fastest | Lowest |\n",
    "| **Regex** | Flexible patterns needed | Medium | Medium |\n",
    "| **Callable** | Complex logic required | Varies | Highest |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Performance Tips\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Start Simple**: Use literal patterns first, add complexity only if needed\n",
    "2. **Optimize Regex**: Use non-capturing groups `(?:...)` when capture isn't needed\n",
    "3. **Test Patterns**: Validate patterns on sample data before deployment\n",
    "4. **Cache Callables**: For expensive operations, cache results in callable functions\n",
    "5. **Profile**: Use `--dryrun` to test patterns before full scans\n",
    "\n",
    "### Common Pitfalls\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Case Sensitivity**: Remember literal patterns are case-sensitive by default\n",
    "2. **Escaping**: Properly escape special characters in regex patterns\n",
    "3. **Greedy Matching**: Use non-greedy quantifiers `*?` and `+?` when appropriate\n",
    "4. **Module Paths**: Callable patterns must be importable Python modules\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Literal patterns** are fast and simple for exact string matches\n",
    "- **Regex patterns** provide flexibility with flags like IGNORECASE\n",
    "- **Callable patterns** enable complex, custom matching logic\n",
    "- Choose pattern types based on complexity vs. performance tradeoffs\n",
    "- Test patterns thoroughly before production deployment\n",
    "\n",
